-- ANIMAUX'26 update (18 Nov): Shark Tank + coaster rules, new brochure PDF. Safe to run more than once.
update public.events
set team_min = 3, team_max = 5, eligibility = 'Teams of 3–5 members, all currently enrolled in college. A student can be in only one team.',
    rules = '["# Format","Up to 7 teams. Live pitches with Q&A and simulated investment negotiations; the top three teams face a surprise challenge.","# Eligibility and teams","Teams must have 3 to 5 members, all currently enrolled in college. A student can be in only one team.","At least 2 members must speak during the pitch, and all members must be present for Q&A.","Mixed-department teams get a bonus (see Bonus points).","# Idea and originality","The idea must be the team’s own work. Copying an existing product or competitor is not allowed. Existing ideas may be improved if the team clearly shows what is new.","The idea must be ethical and animal-safe. Anything that harms, captures, exploits or stresses animals leads to disqualification.","Real data only. Statistics must be accurate and sourced (name the source on the slide). Made-up numbers can lead to a penalty or disqualification.","Teams must not use real brand names or logos in a way that suggests a real partnership or endorsement.","Teams own their ideas. Sharks and organisers may not copy or share them. Photography and filming of pitches is for fest promotion only.","# Event day","Teams must be at the venue 30 minutes before their slot and report to the Backstage Coordinator.","The order of pitches is decided by a draw, and it is final.","A team that is late or absent when called is allowed one grace call (2 minutes). After that it is disqualified and a reserve team steps in.","Teams may use only the materials and equipment listed in the pitching rules below. Extra equipment must be approved by the Head Coordinator at least a day earlier.","No team may interrupt or disturb another team’s pitch. Respect the audience, Sharks and organisers.","Mobile phones are allowed only for the demo or as a timer. No searching for answers during Q&A.","The Head Coordinator’s and the Sharks’ decisions are final.","# Conduct and disqualification","Plagiarism, false claims, harming animals, abusing Sharks or other teams, or sabotage leads to disqualification.","Conflict of interest: a Shark who knows or is related to a team’s member declares it and does not score that team (their score is replaced by the average of the other Sharks).","# Pitching rules: time","3 minutes strictly. A green light at the start, yellow at 2:30, red at 3:00, and a buzzer at 3:15.","Overtime penalty: −1 point per 15 seconds over 3:00. At 3:30 the pitch is stopped.","# Slides and materials","Maximum 8 slides, in PowerPoint or PDF, submitted 24 hours before the event. Slides over the limit lose 2 points.","Bring a backup copy on a pen drive. Videos in the slides must be under 30 seconds in total.","Teams may bring a prototype, poster or demo model (scored under Feasibility). Live animals are not allowed.","Maximum 2 props on stage, set up in 30 seconds or less.","Each team gets one printed Pitch Sheet (A4, one page) for the Sharks, handed in at registration.","# The Ask","The Ask must state the amount (in Wild Dollars), the equity offered (as a %), and how the money will be spent (at least 3 items, with approximate shares).","The Ask must be realistic. Sharks may question inflated valuations and the team must justify them.","The maximum Ask is 10 lakh Wild Dollars (the budget of one Shark). Teams may ask for less.","# Q&A","4 minutes. Sharks ask one question at a time, with a maximum of 2 follow-ups per question.","Only team members may answer. Any member can answer, and the team should share the questions.","“I don’t know” is allowed, but the team should say how they would find out.","No reading from notes or phones.","# Deal round","Each Shark has 10 lakh Wild Dollars for the whole event. They can invest alone or together with other Sharks (co-invest).","A Shark makes an offer as: amount + equity % + one optional condition. Offers must be made within 60 seconds of the Q&A ending.","The team may accept, make one counter-offer, or decline. Negotiation lasts up to 2 minutes.","A team cannot give away more than 100% equity in total across all Sharks.","The Deal Marshal writes every deal on the Deal Sheet and gets it signed by the team captain and the Shark. Only signed deals count.","A Shark may “opt out” at any time, and may say why in one sentence (this feedback helps the team).","# Bonus points (maximum +5 in total)","Mixed departments (team members from 2 or more departments): +2.","Working prototype or live demo that clearly works: +2.","Echoes of the Wild link (a clever use of sound, “echo” or ecology in the idea): +1.","# Penalties","Overtime: −1 per 15 seconds over 3:00.","More than 8 slides: −2.","Unsourced or false statistic: −2 each (up to −6).","Missing the grace call or setup overrun: −2.","# How scores are calculated","Each Shark scores each team on a score sheet immediately after the Deal Round (before the next pitch starts).","With 5 Sharks, the highest and lowest scores are dropped and the remaining 3 are averaged. With 4 Sharks, all 4 are averaged.","Bonus points are added and penalties subtracted by the Scorekeeper.","The Round 2 score is out of 100 (plus bonuses, minus penalties)."]'::jsonb
where slug = 'wild-shark-tank';

update public.events
set rules = '["# Timing","Open from 11:00 AM to 3:30 PM — drop in any time in between.","# Rules and regulations","The event is open to individual participants only. No limit on participants.","Each participant will be provided with one coaster and the necessary basic painting materials.","Participants must create an original artwork based on the theme “Echoes of the Wild”, incorporating elements of wildlife, zoology and forensic investigation.","The artwork must depict or represent a zoological subject, such as an animal, animal anatomy, footprints, feathers, scales, habitats or wildlife conservation.","Participants must incorporate at least one forensic element into their artwork, for example: animal footprints or tracks as forensic evidence; feathers, fur, scales or shed skin as biological evidence; DNA fingerprints or genetic evidence; blood-pattern-inspired investigative illustrations; clues related to wildlife trafficking, poaching or illegal hunting; crime-scene markers and evidence tags.","Participants must give their coaster a suitable title and a short case description (2–3 lines) explaining the story behind their artwork.","All artwork must be completed within the allotted time.","Participants are encouraged to use scientific accuracy while representing animal features, tracks and forensic evidence.","Reference images may be used for inspiration, but copying existing artwork is strictly prohibited.","Participants must maintain cleanliness and avoid damaging the workspace or materials provided.","Use of pre-painted coasters or ready-made designs is not permitted.","The judges’ decision will be final and binding."]'::jsonb
where slug = 'strokes-of-wild';

update public.festival_settings
set data = jsonb_set(data, '{brochureUrl}', '"https://heyzine.com/flip-book/665b121f51.html"'::jsonb)
where id = 1;
